2. PATENT RESTRICTIONS & SCOPE OF PROTECTION
--------------------------------------------
Without limiting the generality of Section 1, the following novel engineering
inventions and technological methods are explicitly protected and reserved:

(a) Thread-Synchronized WebRTC Teardown & Mutex Architecture:
    The method and state machine for preventing race-condition SIGSEGV/SIGBUS
    native memory corruption during asynchronous WebRTC peer connection disposal
    across multi-threaded mobile runtime environments.

(b) Dynamic Adaptive TURN Relay Routing & Single-Pass ICE Policy:
    The network routing architecture utilizing 16,384 dynamic allocation ports
    combined with single-pass (GATHER_ONCE) candidate resolution, removing
    inter-relay round-trip time overhead in mobile and browser voice lounges.

(c) Hardware-Backed Biometric Vault with Zero-Bypass Screen Lock:
    The security protocol binding biometric cryptographic key authentication
    with Android OS screen lock keyguards for zero-bypass offline vault access
    in decentralized messaging clients.

(d) Dual-Tier Rust Audio & Real-Time Broadcast Relay Architecture:
    The concurrent high-throughput message routing methodology interfacing
    a Python application layer with a Rust asynchronous WebSocket engine
    via internal cryptographic secret header validation.

(e) Sliding-Window Stateless Session Renewal with Multi-Alias Synchronization:
    The persistence and recovery mechanism maintaining real-time communication
    integrity and bidirectional SQLite message preservation across transient
    network disconnects and multi-participant channel aliasing.

